       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg per day total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you verified the dose. I'd still recommend checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
